    <td  bgcolor="#c0c0c0" width="100%" valign="top"><tt><font color="#000000">
Author:&nbsp;<a href="/showmember.php?name=Espirius">Espirius</a>&nbsp;(---.001.popsite.net)<br>
Date:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;06-03-01 04:45<br>
<br><HTML>(( i really couldnt think of a subject at 430am))<br>
<br>
I would like to propose a that we begin planned a recruitment phase. (granted im not an officer or anything but.... ) It seems the last few days/weeks NM has undergone some keys changes, as that we've had some popular regular high level people decided to leave the guild. And to be honest... that worries me. Before I came to NM I was one of the last inductees to the Alliance of Druids, the oldest Guild in the Cazic-Thule server (well 2nd oldest ive learned since then) What I see going on now ... parts of it are not dissimilar from what happened when AoD had the floor(s) crumble out from under them. I did not know Kilenn left (who is one of the charter members...why did he leave?) Aluini... Lowbeard... Quick... this has to make a guy say to himself - What are we doing here? Do we need to improve something? Change something? What is our area of opportunity not only for the guild.. but ourselves as well. The officers need to be leaders of the guild. They should be willing to coach and train and mediate any issues anyone should have. Us newbies should realize they have a big job to do, and we can make it easy for them by being patient and not being reckless. Yeah.. okay.. this is a game we are talking about I understand... but in roleplaying if we say we are going to act like a commmunity.. let's do it then. We had a guild raid in unrest this weekend. How many people showed up? i counted 10.. roughly why? did we not plan enough? was there not enough warning? I don't know.<br>
<br>
Supposing we do decide to have a recruitment fiesta.. let's not grab anyone and everyone... garbage in is garbage out. we need to scout... plan.. and make it look like NM is a privledge to be a part of ((Because it is :)  )) not just a guild out to fill the roster again. Which brings me to the next topic: The Roster. <br>
<br>
The post that the officers need to clean up the list on the homepage has been up for a while now... but I don't see it being done. Jiggs can only make it as accurate as we allow him to, which means we need to find out what the deal is with the people we havent seen/heard from in WEEKS. There were people online ..today... which are not yet listed on the member list. Granted we cant say anything but ask nicely that people update their character information, but we should post that too.. perhaps Clunch should make the GMOTD say something to reflect "Dont forget to update your char on the homesite today". I would also vote to do away with the "Outcast" ranking on the member list. It seems ... negative in connotation to me, if they are not members anymore they should be removed from the list entirely unless we'd like to create a 'honorary member' status of some sort. <br>
<br>
To conclude.. this is not a rant or anything of that nature... but I believe that the Norrath Militia seems to have wandered (only in some respects, I really love being a part of this guild) from some of the core values which it began with... and I just want to take a second to make everyone read this twice and think... "Yea......"<br>
<br>
I would invite the officers to challenge themselves to have a meeting in the Live Chat room on our site which no one seems to use (cuz ive poked my head in there  a few times.. ) and discuss some of the things I have mentioned - making action plans where we need directions, and praise where we are doing things right. It needs to be in the regular chat rooms because this meeting should be available to everyone to voice their concerns, needs, opinions, and compliments. It should set the tone for the future of the Norrath Militia. <br>
<br>
Very well. I said what I needed to say (( but if i forgot anything I'll let you know hehe)) Again, it was not my wish to offend anyone with this, but only to grease the wheels, so we can all be better than what we are now. =) <br>
<br>
Espirius</HTML></font></tt><p>
